---
/**
 * M4 How it works, in the legal reading layout. "The loop" and "The call"
 * follow M1's steps at lead length. "How the guides are made" (#totals) is
 * design round 32's disclosure: what's counted, when a figure shows, and
 * who counts. Every disclosure elsewhere links here.
 */
import JsonLd from "@/components/JsonLd.astro";
import VerdictRow from "@/components/VerdictRow.astro";
import { FAQS } from "@/data/content/how-it-works";
import ReadingLayout from "@/layouts/ReadingLayout.astro";
import { faqPage } from "@/lib/jsonLd";

const contents = [
  { id: "the-loop", title: "The loop" },
  { id: "the-verdict", title: "The verdict" },
  { id: "the-call", title: "The call" },
  { id: "totals", title: "How the guides are made" },
  { id: "questions", title: "Questions" },
];
const section = "flex flex-col gap-4";
const h2 = "m-0 type-heading";
---

<ReadingLayout
  title="How it works · dialed.run"
  heading="How it works"
  description="How dialed.run turns what you wore, the weather and how it felt into tomorrow's call."
  contents={contents}
>
  <JsonLd slot="head" node={faqPage(FAQS)} />
  <p slot="lead" class="m-0 type-lead">
    Every run is a measurement: what you wore, what the weather was, and how it
    felt. dialed.run keeps a record per garment and per temperature range, so
    the advice is based on your clothes and how you run warm or cold, not on a
    chart.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="the-loop" class={section}>
    <h2 id="the-loop" class={h2}>
      The loop
    </h2>
    <p class="m-0 type-lead">
      Log the run from Strava or a file, and the weather comes with it, fetched
      for when and where you ran. Then say how it went, from way cold to way
      warm, and which piece was off if one was. That takes ten seconds, and
      every run you log adds to your record.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="the-verdict" class={section}>
    <h2 id="the-verdict" class={h2}>
      The verdict
    </h2>
    <VerdictRow />
    <p class="m-0 text-quiet">
      One tap after the run, plus which piece was off if one was.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="the-call" class={section}>
    <h2 id="the-call" class={h2}>
      The call
    </h2>
    <p class="m-0 type-lead">
      The night before your next run, dialed.run reads the forecast and calls
      your kit from what worked for you at that temperature and in that sky.
      It's your own record, so it knows whether you run warm or cold.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="totals" class={section}>
    <h2 id="totals" class={h2}>
      How the guides are made
    </h2>
    <p class="m-0">
      <strong class="font-semibold">What's counted.</strong> Each run adds its
      feels-like temperature, sky and month, the type, brand and model of each
      piece you wore, and your verdict. Your region counts too, if you've set
      one in Settings. Never your name, handle, notes or photos, and never where
      the run started or the time of day.
    </p>
    <p class="m-0">
      <strong class="font-semibold">When a figure shows.</strong> Every number
      we publish needs at least 5 different runners behind it, or 20 if it's
      about a brand. That goes for every row, section and sentence. Below that,
      the figure is left out. It's never shown as "fewer than 5".
    </p>
    <p class="m-0">
      <strong class="font-semibold">Who counts.</strong> Confirmed accounts
      only. If you've turned off Count my runs in anonymous totals, your runs
      are left out. So are removed entries, banned accounts, accounts being
      deleted, and runs where you set the conditions yourself.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section
    aria-labelledby="questions"
    class="flex flex-col border-t border-ink"
  >
    <h2 id="questions" class="m-0 pt-5 pb-2 type-heading">
      Questions
    </h2>
    {FAQS.map(({ question, answer }) => (
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 border-t border-hairline py-4">
        <h3 class="m-0 type-body font-semibold">{question}</h3>
        <p class="m-0 text-quiet">{answer}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>
</ReadingLayout>
